rust: allow LTO beside BTF again

5daa0c35a1f0 ("rust: Disallow BTF generation with Rust + LTO") kept Rust
out of LTO kernels that generate BTF, because pahole let Rust units
through --lang_exclude when it merged the units of an LTO build. pahole
has filtered them there since b98565e7b17e ("dwarf_loader: Honour
--lang_exclude when merging LTO built CUs"), and the kernel's Rust
objects are not LTO objects, so no Rust type reaches a C unit.

With ThinLTO, vmlinux BTF comes out with no Rust type in it and the
kernel parses it.

--- a/init/Kconfig
+++ b/init/Kconfig
@@ -2065,7 +2065,7 @@
 	depends on !MODVERSIONS || GENDWARFKSYMS
 	depends on !GCC_PLUGIN_RANDSTRUCT
 	depends on !RANDSTRUCT
-	depends on !DEBUG_INFO_BTF || (PAHOLE_HAS_LANG_EXCLUDE && !LTO)
+	depends on !DEBUG_INFO_BTF || PAHOLE_HAS_LANG_EXCLUDE
 	depends on !CFI || HAVE_CFI_ICALL_NORMALIZE_INTEGERS_RUSTC
 	select CFI_ICALL_NORMALIZE_INTEGERS if CFI
 	depends on !KASAN || CC_IS_CLANG
